{"mathcounts-potw-2025-11-10-01":[{"title":"Divide part by whole","body":"Percent = part ÷ whole × 100:\n$$\\frac{18{,}204{,}605}{251{,}047{,}650} \\approx 0.072514 = 7.2514\\%.$$\nTo the nearest hundredth: **7.25%**.\n\n**Answer: 7.25%**"},{"title":"Estimate, then refine","body":"1% of 251,047,650 is about 2,510,477, so 7% is about 17,573,340. The veterans exceed that by about 631,265, which is $631{,}265 \\div 2{,}510{,}477 \\approx 0.25$ of another 1%. So the share is about $7 + 0.25 = 7.25\\%$.\n\n**Answer: 7.25%**"}],"mathcounts-potw-2025-11-10-02":[{"title":"Compute each group","body":"- Korean War: $18{,}204{,}605 \\times 0.081 \\approx 1{,}474{,}573$.\n- WWII: $18{,}204{,}605 \\times 0.034 \\approx 618{,}957$.\n- Difference: $1{,}474{,}573 - 618{,}957 = 855{,}616$.\n\n**Answer: 855,616**"},{"title":"Subtract the percents first","body":"The groups differ by $8.1\\% - 3.4\\% = 4.7\\%$ of all veterans:\n$$18{,}204{,}605 \\times 0.047 = 855{,}616.435 \\approx 855{,}616.$$\n\n**Answer: 855,616**"}],"mathcounts-potw-2025-11-10-03":[{"title":"Find the women's percent","body":"Women made up $100\\% - 91.1\\% = 8.9\\%$ of veterans:\n$$18{,}204{,}605 \\times 0.089 = 1{,}620{,}209.845 \\approx 1{,}620{,}210.$$\n\n**Answer: 1,620,210**"},{"title":"Subtract the men","body":"Men: $18{,}204{,}605 \\times 0.911 \\approx 16{,}584{,}395.2$. Women: $18{,}204{,}605 - 16{,}584{,}395.2 \\approx 1{,}620{,}209.8$, which rounds to 1,620,210.\n\n**Answer: 1,620,210**"}]}